meta {
  name: retry requirement
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/comparisons/{{comparisonId}}/requirements/{{requirementId}}/retry
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: any [200, 409]
}

docs {
  Re-evaluates ONE failed requirement in place. WRITES.

  409 RETRY_NOT_APPLICABLE is correct, not a bug: an extraction-review result is refused because the
  missing clause is upstream of the model, so retrying reaches the same wall. The amended finding
  carries its own prompt and model versions, so a reader can see it was produced separately.
}
